&116 There's no one in this world who can identify you.
&116 这世上没有一个人能认出您。
&117 The past I created for you predetermined you into becoming an assassin.
&117 我为您造的那段过去，早已注定您会成为杀手。
&118 ...But... for some reason... when we sent you out...
&118 ……可是……不知为何……我们把您送出去之后……
&119 ...You betrayed us, Delta-Six.
&119 ……您背叛了我们，Delta-Six。
&120 That wasn't supposed to happen, no it wasn't.
&120 这本不该发生，绝对不该。
&121 And I've spent the last... eight months trying to figure out...
&121 这……八个月来，我一直想弄明白……
&122 Why exactly did my... predestination fail me.
&122 我的……命定安排，究竟为何失灵。
&123 It never has before.
&123 以前从没失灵过。
&334 Azriel... He...
&334 阿兹瑞尔……他……
&124 You know... I've had this theory about you.
&124 您知道吗……我对您有个理论。
&125 About why you totally flipped out and betrayed your fellow assassins, and then turned yourself into the police.
&125 关于您为什么会彻底失控，出卖杀手同伴，然后向警方自首。
&126 You might know a little bit about our operation here, and how you're all designed to be programmed from a clean slate.
&126 您或许多少知道一点我们这儿的运作——所有人都是从一张白纸开始编写出来的。
&127 Funny thing is though, sometimes our patients don't turn out the way we want them to, you being an extreme case.
&127 有趣的是，我们的病人有时并不会长成我们想要的样子——您就是个极端的例子。
&128 Some of them just fail to function as their programmed roles, and you know why?
&128 有些人就是无法按编写好的角色运转，您知道为什么吗？
&129 I think it's because there's one section of the human psyche that we just have never ... deconstructed... in our rehabilitation process.
&129 我想，那是因为人的心智里有一块地方，我们的康复治疗始终无法……解构。
&130 We call it the conscience.
&130 我们管它叫良知。
&131 When you finally pull the trigger, maybe we haven't desensitized you enough to killing.
&131 也许在您最终扣下扳机时，我们还没让您对杀人足够麻木。
&132 Maybe, we need to make you kill innocent men a hundred times over, just like you did in your past.
&132 也许，我们该让您把无辜的人杀上一百遍，就像您从前那样。
&133 You remember it, Azriel. You remember what you did in the Gemini war.
&133 您记得的，阿兹瑞尔。您记得自己在双子星战争里做过什么。
&134 But... sadly... the conscience isn't affected by memories.
&134 可是……可惜……良知不受记忆影响。
&135 It's only affected by experience.
&135 它只受经历影响。
&136 Well, thanks to you, I've decided to integrate a new phase into our rehabilitation process.
&136 好吧，多亏了您，我决定在康复治疗中加入一个新阶段。
&137 This is called deconstructing the conscience, and it will be starting on all patients effective immediately.
&137 这个阶段叫“解构良知”，即刻起对所有病人施行。
&138 And you, Delta-Six, will be the first test subject of this new phase.
&138 而您，Delta-Six，将是这个新阶段的第一个实验对象。
&139 We'll have loads of fun, I'm sure.
&139 我们一定会玩得很开心。
&140 And you, Epsilon-Five... what shall we do with you...?
&140 至于您，Epsilon-Five……我们该拿您怎么办呢……？
&141 Such an unexpected guest deserves some kind of recognition.
&141 这样一位不速之客，总该得到点特别的招待。
&335 ...?
&335 ……？
&142 Goodbye Delta-Six, Epsilon-Five. It was a pleasure to see you both again.
&142 再见了，Delta-Six，Epsilon-Five。能再见到二位，真是荣幸。
&336 It's not working.
&336 不管用。
